    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43803" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐεπής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἔπος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>melodious</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">φωνή</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					X.
					<u>Cyn.</u>
					13.16
				</span></i>
			; <i>euphonious</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λέξις</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.H.
					<u>Comp.</u>
					22
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἁρμονία-εστέρα</span> ibid.
				Adv. -<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">πῶς, κῶλα εὐ.
				συγκείμενα</span> ibid.: 
				Sup.
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ποίησισ-έστατα ἔχουσα</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.Chr.
					52.15
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b>
			<i>eloquent</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">εὐ. ἐν τῷ
			λέγειν</span> Hsch.
				s.v.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λιγύς</span>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>3.</b>
			<i>making eloquent, inspiring</i>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὕδωρ</span>, of Helicon, <i><span class="en">
				<u>AP</u>
				11.24
			</span></i> (Antip.). </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			
				Pass.
			, <i>well-spoken, acceptable</i>, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">λόγος</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Hdt.
					5.50
				</span></i>
			.</div>
